2.6 Strategic Conclusion
The Phase 2 finite-line extraction fails for reasons that are structural, not implementational. None of these blockers exist in the periodic formulation. Phase 3 uses the same Phase 1 dynamic kernel, the same Phase 2 assembly machinery, and the same mesh generator. The only new components are:

A Floquet-periodic Green's function (Ewald or equivalent).

Periodic boundary conditions in z.

Bloch eigenvalue extraction.

The Bloch eigenvalue is unique, well-conditioned, and requires no ports, no de-embedding, no standing-wave fitting, and no N/N+1 subtraction.

Phase 2 has delivered a validated assembly. The extraction is deferred to Phase 3.

